{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"evidence\":[{\"source\":\"李學勤主編《字源》, 2012, 天津古籍出版社 / 辽宁人民出版社, ISBN 9787552800692; source scan inspected directly\",\"field\":\"北部 entry; printed p. 726, PDF p. 739; local scan /home/catalin/hanzi-etymology-books/research-ocr/ziyuan-full/page-0739/source.png; source pixel SHA-256 93340790449e8a235bdf892960bde34eb3ae2a3bc5855f79994ceaa599e0b736\",\"text\":\"The inspected entry calls 北 a *huiyi* graph resembling two people back-to-back and the original graph for 背 (“back/turn against”). It reports Shang oracle use borrowed for the north direction, citing inscriptions 合集8783 and 合集32030. The author says frequent use for north led to the later addition of 肉 in 背, leaving 北 chiefly for north. Printed page number 726 is visible in the scan; the entry is on PDF page 739. The cited inscription contexts were not independently checked here.\",\"record_character\":\"北\",\"kind\":\"local_book_scan_inspected\",\"url\":\"https://search.worldcat.org/search?q=9787552800692\",\"title\":\"字源\",\"accessed_at\":\"2026-10-03\"},{\"source\":\"Zhengzhou University Center for Chinese Character Civilization, Chen Anqi\",\"field\":\"graphic_history_and_original_sense\",\"text\":\"The study describes the form from Shang inscriptions through the Shuowen seal form as two people back-to-back, with changes in stroke execution. It proposes an original word meaning “turn against/violate,” while acknowledging no secure excavated example has been identified; two proposed Zhouyi examples remain uncertain. This is an interpretation of the graphic conception and later written evidence, not a demonstrated earliest spoken sense.\",\"record_character\":\"北\",\"kind\":\"paleographic_study\",\"url\":\"https://www5.zzu.edu.cn/hzwm/info/1168/1868.htm\",\"title\":\"“北”字职用演变研究（一）\",\"accessed_at\":\"2026-10-03\"},{\"source\":\"Zhengzhou University Center for Chinese Character Civilization, Chen Anqi\",\"field\":\"earliest_attested_sense_and_graph_borrowing\",\"text\":\"The author reports 北 used from the Shang period as a loan graph for the direction “north,” its continuing principal function. The study distinguishes this from proposed extensions of an inferred “turn against” word. Thus the graphic history, a proposed original word sense, and the attested use of the graph for north are separate claims.\",\"record_character\":\"北\",\"kind\":\"scholarly_study\",\"url\":\"https://www5.zzu.edu.cn/hzwm/info/1168/1864.htm\",\"title\":\"“北”字职用演变研究（三）\",\"accessed_at\":\"2026-10-03\"},{\"source\":\"Zhengzhou University Center for Chinese Character Civilization, Chen Anqi\",\"field\":\"graphic_differentiation_of_背\",\"text\":\"The study reports 北 used for “back” in Qin–Han manuscripts while the graph 背, formed with 肉 as semantic element and 北 as phonetic, emerged around the Qin–Han transition. An early Western Han Zhangjiashan manuscript still uses 北 more often for “back”; by Eastern Han evidence 背 is the usual graph. This describes writing practices, not the origin date of the spoken word.\",\"record_character\":\"北\",\"kind\":\"scholarly_study\",\"url\":\"https://www5.zzu.edu.cn/hzwm/info/1168/1868.htm\",\"title\":\"“北”字职用演变研究（一）\",\"accessed_at\":\"2026-10-03\"},{\"source\":\"Zhengzhou University Center for Chinese Character Civilization, Chen Anqi\",\"field\":\"semantic_extensions_and_attestations\",\"text\":\"The author proposes paths from “turn against” to bodily back and back side, and further to concealment, betrayal, abandonment, military defeat/flight, and defeated troops. The article provides Qin–Han manuscript examples for bodily back and back side and discusses other excavated or transmitted examples. Some steps rely on transmitted-text spellings or proposed semantic links; this evidence does not establish a complete chronology of spoken senses.\",\"record_character\":\"北\",\"kind\":\"scholarly_study\",\"url\":\"https://www5.zzu.edu.cn/hzwm/info/1168/1868.htm\",\"title\":\"“北”字职用演变研究（一）\",\"accessed_at\":\"2026-10-03\"}],\"search_audit\":[{\"query\":\"北 character oracle bone Shang back-to-back paleography 背 study Chen Anqi\",\"urls\":[\"https://museum.sinica.edu.tw/en/exhibitions/13/\",\"https://rub.ihp.sinica.edu.tw/~oracle/02_1.htm\",\"https://rub.ihp.sinica.edu.tw/~oracle/01_2.htm\",\"https://dap.ihp.sinica.edu.tw/en/database/3/\",\"https://www5.zzu.edu.cn/hzwm/info/1168/1868.htm\"],\"outcome\":\"Search returned institutional oracle-bone resources and the Zhengzhou University study; opened the study and read its discussion of form, uncertain original sense, and excavated examples.\"},{\"query\":\"北 字源 董莲池 乖背之背 初文 甲骨文 商代\",\"urls\":[\"https://www5.zzu.edu.cn/hzwm/info/1168/1868.htm\",\"https://www5.zzu.edu.cn/hzwm/info/1168/1864.htm\"],\"outcome\":\"Inspected the Zhengzhou University study pages for claims on original sense, north-direction borrowing, and later differentiation of 背.\"},{\"query\":\"北 oracle bone inscriptions earliest north loan graph character dictionary Academia Sinica\",\"urls\":[\"https://www5.zzu.edu.tw/hzwm/info/1168/1868.htm\",\"https://ytenx.org/kyonh/sieux/3735/\",\"https://www.unicode.org/cgi-bin/GetUnihanData.pl?codepoint=5317\"],\"outcome\":\"Inspected the Zhengzhou University research and attempted the Guangyun and official Unihan pages. YTenx returned an internal error; Unihan page returned no usable content. Local full Unihan and Baxter–Sagart source files were absent at the checked repository paths.\"}],\"gaps\":[\"The 字源 scan page directly inspected is PDF p. 739 / printed p. 726. Its entry is correctly headed 北; no OCR transcription error requiring correction was seen in the relevant prose. Printed page metadata was null in the provisional corpus, although p. 726 is legible in the scan.\",\"The cited 字源 oracle examples 合集8783 and 合集32030 were not independently opened in an inscription database; the book's report is citable as its own claim, not independent confirmation of those contexts.\",\"The proposed original sense “turn against/violate” remains unconfirmed by secure excavated examples according to Chen Anqi; do not present it as an established earliest sense. The hypothesized semantic connection of that word with “north” is a proposal, while north-direction use is reported from Shang times.\",\"[SCAN VERIFICATION REQUIRED] 字源 PDF p. 739 / printed p. 726 shows a sequence of historical glyph specimens labeled 商, 西周, 春秋, 战国, 小篆, 汉, and 楷书. The surrounding entry text and headings were read, but individual specimen identities were not separately checked against the cited source works. Do not use a specific specimen as independent evidence without targeted verification.\",\"Official Unicode Unihan record for 北 was attempted at https://www.unicode.org/cgi-bin/GetUnihanData.pl?codepoint=5317 but returned no usable page text; the harness-provided local kMandarin value běi is not independently verified here. No exact local Unihan or Baxter–Sagart table row was available at the expected repository paths.\"]}"}}
